#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""board-mcp: the agent board as a Model Context Protocol server over stdio.

Python 3.10+, standard library only. Started by an MCP client (`claude mcp add`, or the plugin in
this directory). It speaks newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdin/stdout, logs only to stderr, and
does every database operation by running the `board` helper (an argv list, never a shell), so the SQL,
the lease rules and the fence rules exist in exactly one place (integrations/board/board).

Identity and secrets
  The author of every write is BOARD_AUTHOR in this process's environment. No tool argument can set
  it. Connection settings (LATTICE_BOARD_URL, PG*) are read by the helper from the environment and are
  never printed, echoed or put in a result. Helper messages are classified; only a few fixed texts and
  the helper's own one-line complaints reach a result, with credentials and fence numbers removed.

Leases
  board_next and board_claim return an opaque lease_id. The server keeps the fence behind it, in memory
  and in a private state file (crash recovery only), and passes it to the helper with --fence on every write.
  No tool takes a fence and the server never returns one as a field (the number is not a secret: it is the claim
  event's id). A lease_id belongs to this server process. One this server does not know is refused before anything is written; a
  lease the board no longer honours (helper exit 3) is refused by the board and forgotten here.

Untrusted text
  Titles, bodies and notes were written by other agents or people. They are returned as data: control
  characters stripped, length bounded, inside a block marked with a random token in the text content,
  and under an "untrusted" member in structuredContent. Nothing here interprets them.

Protocol: the 2026-07-28 revision (no handshake, `_meta` on every request, `server/discover`) and the
2025-11-25 handshake (`initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, `ping`), the same rules as the gateway
(docs/mcp-v0.md). Documentation: integrations/board/CONVENTIONS.md, "board-mcp".
"""

